# Split-test weights: seconds of go test -race Elapsed per top-level test name,
# summed over the split packages (scripts/go-test-split-packages) that have
# the name. scripts/go-test-non-runtime-shards deals split test names to the
# split shards heaviest first, each to the lightest shard so far, so a slow
# test does not land beside other slow tests by the luck of discovery order.
# A name not listed here weighs 1. The weights only balance; a stale or
# missing line never drops or repeats a test (go-shard-discovery-test).
# Source: CI run 40138087758 (2026-10-24), split shards 0-5, race. Refresh
# from a recent run's go test -json logs when a shard becomes the outlier
# again; names under 3 s are left out. TestEventTableTrajectoryWindowOverTenThousand
# was 489 s before it filled its three stores in parallel; 170 is an estimate.
